state.updated_at` (or `now \u003e= state.updated_at`; ignore backward time `now \u003c state.updated_at` completely without lowering `updated_at`), compute `state.tokens = min(state.capacity, state.tokens + (now - state.updated_at) * state.refill_rate)` using pure `Decimal` arithmetic (no `float`), and set `state.updated_at = now`.\n  - `TokenBucket.consume`: Validate `amount = as_decimal(amount)` and `amount \u003c= 0` -\u003e `ValueError(\"amount must be positive\")` before calling `self.refill(now)`.\n- **`registry.py`**:\n  - `BucketRegistry.__init__`: Remove mutable default `buckets={}`; initialize `self._buckets = {}` (or `dict(buckets)` if `buckets=None` is kept, or simply `def __init__(self, clock=time.monotonic): self.clock = clock; self._buckets = {}`).\n  - `BucketRegistry.add`: Key by `(tenant_id, name)`. If `key in self._buckets`, raise `ValueError(\"duplicate bucket\")` without replacing. Otherwise create `TokenBucket(capacity, refill_rate, self.clock)`, store at `self._buckets[key]`, and return it.\n  - `BucketRegistry.get`: Return `self._buckets[(tenant_id, name)]` (raises `KeyError` if missing).\n- **`middleware.py`**:\n  - `RateLimiter.consume`: Materialize `requests` (e.g. `list(requests)` to support generators). If empty, return `True`.\n  - Validate every `(name, amount)` pair: convert `amount = as_decimal(amount)` and require `amount \u003e 0` (`ValueError` if invalid/non-positive), and resolve `bucket = self.registry.get(tenant_id, name)` (`KeyError` if missing) — all before any mutation.\n  - Aggregate required amounts per `name` (or per bucket) for repeated bucket names.\n  - Sample `now = self.registry.clock()` once for the non-empty request.\n  - Snapshot `(bucket.state.tokens, bucket.state.updated_at)` for all participating buckets before mutating.\n  - Refill each participating bucket once at `now` (`bucket.refill(now)`).\n  - Check if every participating bucket has `bucket.state.tokens \u003e= total_needed[name]`.\n  - On `False` or any exception during refill/check/deduct, restore all participating buckets' `state.tokens` and `state.updated_at` to their exact pre-request snapshots and return `False` (or re-raise on exception).\n  - On success, deduct `total_needed[name]` from each participating bucket's `state.tokens` and return `True`.\n\n### Verify Command\n- `pytest -q --tb=short`\n","duration_seconds":13.774569,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":28300,"output_tokens":1749,"thinking_tokens":113,"cache_read_tokens":22158,"total_tokens":30049}}}
